@startuml ThreeTierEdit
' title:    3-tier web app (edit-existing demo)
' type:     Container
' level:    2
' mode:     strict
' audience: Engineering team
' question: How do you edit a pre-existing diagram (add a node, re-route, preserve layout)?
' adr:      n/a
' Worked example for SKILL.md section "Editing an existing diagram".
'
' Scenario: the user already has the 3-tier diagram below (Front Door,
' App Service, SQL Database) and asks to add a Redis cache between the
' app tier and the database.
'
' The edit is a minimal diff against the original: it preserves the
' startuml diagram name, the skinparam block, the cluster structure, and
' the alias style. Only the redis rectangle and its two edges were added.
'
' Wrong approach: re-author from scratch and re-flow the layout, which
' loses the user tuning and yields an unreviewable diff.
' Right approach: add one rectangle for the cache (filename looked up in
' the Azure INDEX as Databases/AzureRedisCache.png) plus two edges.

top to bottom direction
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam defaultFontName "Inter, Arial, sans-serif"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor transparent
  BorderColor transparent
  FontColor #1F2937
}

rectangle "Azure 3-tier web app" as app {
  rectangle "<img:https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hanv89/archicon/main/dist/Azure/Networking/AzureFrontDoor.png>\nAzure Front Door" as fd
  rectangle "<img:https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hanv89/archicon/main/dist/Azure/Compute/AzureAppService.png>\nApp Service" as app_svc
  rectangle "<img:https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hanv89/archicon/main/dist/Azure/Databases/AzureSqlDatabase.png>\nAzure SQL Database" as sql
  rectangle "<img:https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hanv89/archicon/main/dist/Azure/Databases/AzureRedisCache.png>\nCache for Redis" as redis
}

fd --> app_svc : "HTTPS"
app_svc --> sql : "OLTP reads/writes"
app_svc --> redis : "cache reads"
redis --> sql : "cache-miss fill"

@enduml
